      "why": ".plot() with no kind= draws a line, and it plots against the index — so putting the dates in the index is what makes the x-axis a timeline.",
      "whenToUse": "A first look at how one metric moves over time.",
      "commonMistake": "Calling .plot() without setting the date index, which plots against 0, 1, 2… instead of dates.",
